meta {
  name: auth
  seq: 2
}

docs {
  Login, refresh, logout — and, added in Phase 3, the security center's
  self-service session list/revocation and self-service password reset.

  Sessions: login-secondary and login-tertiary open two more sessions
  under the same admin account (a stand-in for "another device"), without
  touching accessToken/refreshToken — the primary login from login.bru
  keeps authenticating every request in this folder, including logout at
  the very end. revoke-session revokes the secondary one specifically, by
  the session_id login itself returns; revoke-other-sessions then revokes
  everything but the primary, which by that point is only the tertiary
  login.

  Password reset: password-reset-request only ever proves the endpoint
  answers 202 — the response deliberately never contains the token (that
  is the whole point, see RequestPasswordReset's own doc comment), and
  this collection has no mailbox to read one out of an email, so nothing
  here can exercise a successful confirm. errors/
  password-reset-confirm-invalid-token.bru covers the confirm endpoint's
  failure shape instead.
}
